Rule 1 (two-tensor inputs must be broadcastable per-dimension; prevents size-mismatch error)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : (shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)) ∨ (shape(v_1, i) = 1) ∨ (shape(v_2, i) = 1)
>>
Rule 2 (comparison not supported for complex tensors; prevents "le_cpu not implemented for ComplexDouble")
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (dtype_(v_1) ≠ 9 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 10) ∧ (dtype_(v_2) ≠ 9 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≠ 10)
>>
Rule 3 (with out for tensor-tensor: out is bool tensor with broadcasted shape; prevents invalid out type and size-mismatch)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ndim(v_3) = ndim(v_1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : ((shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)) ∨ (shape(v_1, i) = 1) ∨ (shape(v_2, i) = 1)) ∧ if shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) then shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_1, i) else if shape(v_1, i) = 1 then shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_2, i) else shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_1, i) ∧ dtype_(v_3) = 0
